+++ b/docs/task-list-api.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Task list API specification
+
+Version: 1.0
+
+## Stable task identifiers
+
+Requirement: a task remains addressable after it is renamed.
+
+Each `Task` returned by `TaskList.add` has an `id` string. A list assigns IDs in insertion order as
+`task-1`, `task-2`, and so on. An ID is never reused by that list, including after removal. This makes
+the identifiers deterministic while ensuring that no two tasks returned by the same list share an ID.
+
+`TaskList.get(id)` looks up only an ID and returns the usual `Result<Task>` outcome. `find`,
+`complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`, and `remove` each accept either an ID or a title. When
+a string could name both an ID and a title, it is interpreted as an ID so a task is always reachable by
+its stable identifier.
